  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Knowledge and Capacity on the Migration and Climate Change Nexus in South-East Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The action will support the Global Compact for Safe, Orderly, and Regular Migration (GCM) by enhancing data management, addressing migration drivers, reducing vulnerabilities, developing skills, and fostering international cooperation. It will also contribute to the Paris Agreement on Climate Change, the ASEAN-EU Strategic Partnership Plan of Action (2023-2027), and several Sustainable Development Goals.The action aims to achieve the following outcomes:EVIDENCE: Improved evidence on climate-induced migration is made available for policymaking at regional, national, and sub-national levels amongst the selected ASEAN countries. POLICY: Improved policy action and initiatives on climate adaptation and migration management aimed at reducing risks for vulnerable populations of all genders and ages in the targeted ASEAN countries. ASEAN ENGAGEMENT: Improved inclusion of climate-induced migration evidence and policy approaches in regional and multilateral dialogues and ASEAN governance initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
